module

public import ThreeCopyQutritWerner.Basic

@[expose] public section


/-!
# The reduced statement of the symmetry-reduction bridge

This module fixes, as concrete finite definitions, the symmetry-reduced coordinates in which the
T2.1a certificate is checked, and states the bridge in that form (`X2ReducedBridge`). It follows the
certificate's exact computation entry for entry.

Conventions.
* Sectors `s : Fin 3`: `0 = h` (holomorphic), `1 = m` (mixed), `2 = a` (antiholomorphic).
* Local types `t : Fin 8` (sectors h and a have seven types; type 7 has multiplicity 0 there).
  `x2Mult s t` is the multiplicity (number of integer frame columns `U_{s,t}`), `x2IrrepDim s t`
  the irrep dimension, `x2Gram s t = U_{s,t}ᵀ U_{s,t}`.
* Blocks (keys) of sector `s`: `x2Key s = Fin 122 | Fin 169 | Fin 123`, in the order of
  the certificate's image list. Key `b` has sorted types `x2KeyTypes s b`, stabilizer kind, S3 degree and
  size `r_b = x2KeySize s b`. Its ambient (tensor product of local multiplicity spaces) is
  `x2Amb s b = Fin m₀ × Fin m₁ × Fin m₂`; the image `J_b : x2Amb s b → Fin r_b` is data.
* Every block matrix is in *Q-form* (quadratic-form) coordinates: for an invariant operator `X`
  the Q-form on block `b` is `W_bᵀ X W_b` with `W_b = (U_{t₀} ⊗ U_{t₁} ⊗ U_{t₂}) J_b`.
* Source blocks `N b` (sectors m, a) are *coefficient* matrices in `J`-coordinates: the trial is
  `N b = K Z Zᵀ Kᵀ / 2^160`. The physical operator of a block is its invariant extension; on the
  canonical arrangement its local Q-form is `GJ N GJᵀ` (`GJ = (G ⊗ G ⊗ G) J`) plus, for S3 degree
  2, the standard-copy partner `(1/3) P GJ N (P GJ)ᵀ` with `P = (cyclic shift) - (cyclic shift)²`
  (the certificate's `input_raw` multiplies both by 3; here the physical normalization is used, so that
  `x2Out = output_s / output_denominator_s` of the certificate's archive). Other site arrangements of the
  types are read from the canonical block through the site permutations, averaged
  (`x2FullTensor`), so the source operator is S3-invariant for any data.
* Parity coordinates: per site the 513 local Q-form units `(t, a, b)` split into 282 symmetric
  labels (`a ≤ b`, `x2SLabel`) and 231 antisymmetric labels (`a < b`, `x2ALabel`), in the certificate's layout.
  A real symmetric S3-invariant three-site Q-form is stored as `S : 282³` and `A : 282 × 231²`
  (symmetric site first). The transfer is `S ↦ (Rs ⊗ Rs ⊗ Rs) S`, `A ↦ (Rs ⊗ Ra ⊗ Ra) A`, with
  `Rs, Ra` the diagonal blocks of `N₀ R_s⁻¹ Niₛ` (exact rationals; data).
* The target is `T_b = J_bᵀ (⊗ᵢ (G_{tᵢ} - D_{tᵢ}/2)) J_b` with `D_t` the Q-form of `Ω₀₅`
  (`x2SwapDiagram`), and the residual Q-form is `T_b - out^m_b - out^a_b` (`x2Residual`).

This module contains definitions only. The statement `X2ReducedBridge D` (PSD source blocks and PSD
residual blocks imply T2.1a) is a definition here; `x2ReducedBridge_concrete_of_keys` (CertificateX2FinalCurrent)
proves it for the concrete data from the key frame facts.
-/

